title: A session says what it holds with 'pacer.sh hold', and the hold lapses when its Claude process ends.
pid: 8f83d3ce-0e27-4d53-a298-b5ea01a2879a
body: |2-
  Built 2026-11-14 for Top, so that a session talking with Jeff and a
  session the pacer started do not collide. 'pacer.sh holds' says who
  holds what; 'pacer.sh hold WHAT...' adds to this session's hold, and
  refuses, holding nothing, if another session holds any of it;
  'pacer.sh release [WHAT...]' lets go of some or all. The words are
  free: 'graph' is Top's graph, 'code' the working tree, a specialist's
  name its graph. The pacer starts no session while another holds
  'graph', which replaces 'pause' and needs no 'resume'.
contains:
- bb1710df-83f1-4854-9928-f096b2701432
